    "body": "Closes #1993\n\nA C array of extension type objects as a cdef class member crashes the compiler right after the correct error:\n\n```\n5:17: Array element cannot be a Python object\nAttributeError: 'PyExtensionType' object has no attribute 'create_to_py_utility_code'\n```\n\n`CArrayDeclaratorNode.analyse` reports the error but still builds the array type from the Python object type. For a cdef class member, `_inject_pickle_methods` then asks that array type for a to-Python converter, and the array asks its element type, which has none.\n\nThe element type now falls back to `error_type` after the error, the same way the template parameter error a few lines up does. Before, the crash also hid errors further down the file, like a `cdef A arr[2]` local in a later function. The test covers an extension type member, an `object` member and a function local.\n\nThe `errors` tests and the `run` tests for arrays, pickling and cdef classes pass.\n",
